  "recommendations": [
    "Register a Flux-owned gated map proxy through Polestar.MapCanvas.Add once per map; add no Polestar dependency and call only when the optional capability is present.",
    "Use Flux-owned frame objects created without Blizzard parent, then parent them under canvas/viewport, following Polestar's stated gamepad taint avoidance; never place plugin-owned values in Blizzard map pools or providers.",
    "Because Add has no Remove, own both canvas and viewport visibility gates, so disabling Map Pins hides all Polestar content and stops child updates without touching Polestar preferences.",
    "Forward read methods with actual BattlefieldMapFrame receiver; account for missing Classic HasZoomLevels and existing zoom capability differences.",
    "Keep generic standard pin support separate from Polestar registration. Public addon-owned active pins can be read into Flux-owned paint snapshots without AcquirePin/global/provider replacement.",
    "Arbitrary addon direct frames cannot be guaranteed without an exposed registration API or source-aware geometry; a hidden world map with a different mapID cannot provide fresh battlefield content generically without mutating source state."
  ],
